      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The nationwide public push for sweeping changes in the care of the dying has highlighted dissatisfaction with the way end-of-life care is provided in critical care units. This paper addresses barriers to improving that care, and suggests assessments and strategies that nurses could use to improve quality in this important area."},
